WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:127826

1
00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:02.736
We now have a roadmap with features.

2
00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:06.406
But how do we build them? With specs of course,

3
00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.908
starting with the first roadmap feature.

4
00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:12.012
Let's take a look at the AgentClinic roadmap.

5
00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:15.849
Here's our phase one feature, Hello Hono.

6
00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.518
But it's too early to start coding.

7
00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:22.055
We need to discuss the spec and clarify all the details.

8
00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.524
A good plan outlines the approach,

9
00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:28.028
the sequence of work, and how to validate success.

10
00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.231
Let's start with fresh agent context.

11
00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.600
The agent can get what it

12
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.935
needs from the official source, the constitution.

13
00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:39.205
We will work on this feature in a separate branch,

14
00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:41.307
which we will indicate to the agent.

15
00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:45.445
Our prompt will help start a conversation with the agent

16
00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:48.348
about the feature spec, a plan for tasks,

17
00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:51.851
collect requirements, and a scorecard for validation.

18
00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.788
The agent will ask you to make key decisions.

19
00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:58.091
Pay attention to potential conflicts or problems.

20
00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:02.195
You don't have to agree with the solutions proposed by the agent.

21
00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.498
Make sure to clarify anything that bothers you.

22
00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.068
First, regarding phase one scope,

23
00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.470
we'll keep it exactly as written.

24
00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.773
For the requirements, let's pin the Hono version

25
00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:16.076
and enforce strict TypeScript.

26
00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.579
For the confirmation, manual curl looks good.

27
00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.649
Then, let's submit.

28
00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:28.721
That was fast. Must have been a nano.

29
00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.125
Work is done and the ball is back on our side

30
00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:35.128
for reviewing the feature spec created by the agent.

31
00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.931
Let's review the feature plan first.

32
00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.334
It's important to get these docs right in the beginning

33
00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.336
to keep the agent on track.

34
00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:46.739
If you find something wrong, ask the agent to fix it,

35
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.243
to make sure it keeps the requirements and validation in sync.

36
00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:54.881
For example, we would like a nice looking placeholder home

37
00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.950
page in this first feature spec.

38
00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.452
We make the change via the agent.

39
00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.956
Next, the requirements.

40
00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.758
These were also updated to reflect the homepage update.

41
00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.394
This is the right place to

42
00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.763
indicate any important technical needs or constraints.

43
00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.966
Don't speed through this,

44
00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:17.770
but don't state minor technical details like variable names here.

45
00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.206
We want to control the process

46
00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:24.310
but not oversteer the agent. Last, the validation.

47
00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:27.914
Make sure the agent can check that it got it right.

48
00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:30.884
Again, these were updated for the homepage.

49
00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:32.886
We're done with the feature spec.

50
00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.888
Let's create a commit in the IDE.

51
00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.594
Nice. We formulated a feature spec strategy.

52
00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:43.897
Made a feature branch, interviewed with the

53
00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.899
agent about what the feature should do.

54
00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:48.601
Put the results in markdown documents,

55
00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:51.604
reviewed these spec files, committed.

56
00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.908
The changes you make here in the specs

57
00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:58.278
will expand downstream into hundreds of lines of code.

58
00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:01.281
So time spent here is well spent.

59
00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.183
It's time for implementation.
